1
00:00:49,020 --> 00:00:53,000
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,310 --> 00:00:55,960
[Episode 25]

3
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:32,940
[Golden Imperial Dance Hall]

4
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:38,500
Dong, this is definitely
Zhao Changyou's stash.

5
00:01:38,970 --> 00:01:41,380
We found it at Mi's Mountain Produce Store
in the eastern suburbs.

6
00:01:41,630 --> 00:01:42,830
We intercepted it.

7
00:01:43,050 --> 00:01:43,770
Give me the phone.

8
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:46,640
Go outside first.

9
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:48,780
Out. Get out.

10
00:01:57,180 --> 00:01:58,970
Hey, Mi.

11
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,230
Who sold you

12
00:02:02,690 --> 00:02:03,790
that tiger penis?

13
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:07,140
A tall, skinny young man.

14
00:02:07,780 --> 00:02:09,550
Looked like a real tough guy.

15
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:11,430
Had a look in his eyes

16
00:02:11,430 --> 00:02:12,750
like he could eat you alive.

17
00:02:14,370 --> 00:02:15,740
All right. Got it.

18
00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:23,030
Young,

19
00:02:23,910 --> 00:02:25,680
tall and skinny,

20
00:02:26,810 --> 00:02:28,750
with a pretty intimidating stare.

21
00:02:31,290 --> 00:02:32,780
Who could that be?

22
00:02:35,030 --> 00:02:36,920
This is my buddy.
The ride-or-die kind.

23
00:02:36,950 --> 00:02:38,460
We've been friends
since we were in diapers.

24
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:39,360
He's looking for a job.

25
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:40,520
San Yan'er is good-for-nothing.

26
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:42,100
I was afraid you'd think I'm useless too.

27
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:43,530
I'll take the job.

28
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:45,870
You really killed Li Dewu?

29
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:48,550
Pay me.

30
00:04:06,870 --> 00:04:07,340
Hey,

31
00:04:08,030 --> 00:04:08,520
it's me.

32
00:04:09,370 --> 00:04:11,090
I have a dinner engagement tonight.

33
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:12,930
Go ahead and eat without me.

34
00:04:13,250 --> 00:04:14,000
I'll be home later.

35
00:04:27,770 --> 00:04:29,200
[Tiecheng Warmhearted Senior Care Home]

36
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:31,380
[Address: No. 7, Fuanli, Old Street Road,
Tiecheng]

37
00:04:29,930 --> 00:04:30,920
Here, sweetheart.

38
00:05:23,510 --> 00:05:24,800
This nursing home

39
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:26,620
is just a bus ride away on Route 7.

40
00:05:27,430 --> 00:05:29,330
It costs 500 to 800 yuan a month.

41
00:05:30,740 --> 00:05:32,680
The director is a veteran.

42
00:05:35,450 --> 00:05:36,930
While I'm still clear-headed,

43
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:38,870
let me tell you something, sweetheart.

44
00:05:40,270 --> 00:05:42,450
You stayed at our place
after you got married

45
00:05:42,690 --> 00:05:43,510
because

46
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:45,870
Liu Yang had a guest staying there.

47
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:47,750
Once the guest leaves,

48
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:51,450
you'll have to move back there, won't you?

49
00:05:53,370 --> 00:05:54,180
I'm not going.

50
00:05:54,950 --> 00:05:56,790
With two sick people under one roof,

51
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:00,000
no matter how good your husband is,

52
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:02,120
he won't be able to handle it.

53
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:05,270
Give this house to Xiaopeng.

54
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:07,620
He'll need it when he gets married.

55
00:06:08,450 --> 00:06:10,240
I'm perfectly fine at the nursing home.

56
00:06:12,430 --> 00:06:13,010
I...

57
00:06:16,890 --> 00:06:17,620
Sweetheart,

58
00:06:20,950 --> 00:06:22,750
I've wronged you all my life.

59
00:06:25,250 --> 00:06:27,420
It's too late for me to regret it now.

60
00:06:29,750 --> 00:06:32,680
My mind comes and goes.

61
00:06:33,890 --> 00:06:35,120
I don't want to be a burden to you.

62
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:37,870
Things are already messed up enough.

63
00:06:40,130 --> 00:06:41,680
One more burden won't make a difference.

64
00:06:44,950 --> 00:06:46,430
Hao Peng is a good-for-nothing

65
00:06:47,430 --> 00:06:48,740
with no future anyway.

66
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:51,600
And with me being this sick,

67
00:06:52,420 --> 00:06:53,060
I'd be better off dead

68
00:06:53,930 --> 00:06:55,370
than alive.

69
00:06:57,330 --> 00:06:58,650
All these years,

70
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:01,330
you had every chance to change your mind.

71
00:07:02,370 --> 00:07:03,370
Plenty of chances

72
00:07:03,370 --> 00:07:05,270
to take the two of us back to Shanghai.

73
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:06,870
But what did you do?

74
00:07:09,850 --> 00:07:11,870
Just to prove a point,

75
00:07:13,250 --> 00:07:15,500
you ruined both of your children's lives.

76
00:07:20,910 --> 00:07:22,510
Stop trying to make yourself feel better.

77
00:07:23,870 --> 00:07:25,720
No one is going to thank you for this.

78
00:07:26,550 --> 00:07:28,750
Nothing you do can change the fact

79
00:07:29,450 --> 00:07:30,810
that you're selfish.

80
00:07:30,810 --> 00:07:31,370
No,

81
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:32,320
no.

82
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:33,630
Sweetheart...

83
00:07:34,230 --> 00:07:35,720
Take it back.

84
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,740
There's hardly any money in this passbook.

85
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:41,430
There is money, sweetheart.

86
00:07:41,830 --> 00:07:43,180
Look. See?

87
00:07:43,180 --> 00:07:44,030
It's all here.

88
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:46,560
Stop pretending. Just stop.

89
00:07:46,590 --> 00:07:49,159
No, sweetheart, you...

90
00:07:49,770 --> 00:07:51,530
You said your throat hurt, remember?

91
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:53,570
Your exams are coming up, so you must
have gotten too much internal heat, right?

92
00:07:53,570 --> 00:07:55,300
That's got to be it.

93
00:07:55,390 --> 00:07:57,040
Look, I got you some

94
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:58,490
Longdan Xiegan Pills.

95
00:07:58,680 --> 00:07:59,240
I...

96
00:08:00,390 --> 00:08:03,060
W-Where did I put the medicine?

97
00:08:03,130 --> 00:08:04,910
Wait, I'll find them for you.

98
00:08:05,890 --> 00:08:07,560
I... that medicine...

99
00:08:13,450 --> 00:08:14,630
Where did I put those pills?

100
00:08:16,630 --> 00:08:18,560
Longdan Xiegan Pills.

101
00:08:19,950 --> 00:08:20,870
Mom,

102
00:08:22,180 --> 00:08:23,680
stop looking.

103
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:26,400
My throat is okay now.

104
00:08:28,430 --> 00:08:29,290
Wait...

105
00:08:29,660 --> 00:08:31,270
Where did I put them?

106
00:08:31,270 --> 00:08:32,340
Stop looking.

107
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:37,340
Stop looking.

108
00:08:39,669 --> 00:08:40,890
Stop looking.

109
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:46,630
Careful. Be careful.

110
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:47,510
Director.

111
00:08:49,340 --> 00:08:49,890
Back up.

112
00:08:50,010 --> 00:08:50,650
Ms. Chen.

113
00:08:50,770 --> 00:08:51,340
Back up.

114
00:08:51,500 --> 00:08:52,440
Make sure you've checked

115
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:54,010
where this batch is being shipped.

116
00:08:54,010 --> 00:08:54,980
Don't mix anything up.

117
00:08:54,980 --> 00:08:55,840
No problem, Ms. Chen.

118
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:56,890
This is to Taiyuan.

119
00:08:56,890 --> 00:08:57,510
This is to Zhengzhou.

120
00:08:57,770 --> 00:08:58,660
All right.

121
00:08:58,840 --> 00:08:59,570
Be careful.

122
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:00,610
Don't worry.

123
00:09:02,150 --> 00:09:03,480
Be careful, everyone.

124
00:09:03,510 --> 00:09:05,040
Everyone, stay safe.

125
00:09:06,130 --> 00:09:07,390
Stop unloading. Stop unloading.

126
00:09:07,390 --> 00:09:08,170
Here. Come here.

127
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,580
Something is wrong with this shipment.
Contact the manufacturer right away.

128
00:09:10,580 --> 00:09:11,460
Smell this.

129
00:09:13,010 --> 00:09:13,960
It smells sour.

130
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:14,840
It's all gone sour.

131
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:16,250
Who knows how long this stuff
has been sitting around?

132
00:09:16,250 --> 00:09:17,660
The antioxidants inside have already
lost their effectiveness.

133
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:19,420
Stop unloading. Stop unloading.

134
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:20,670
Baldy, stop unloading it.
Put it back in the truck.

135
00:09:20,670 --> 00:09:21,150
Stop. Stop. Stop.

136
00:09:21,170 --> 00:09:21,870
Stop. Stop. Stop.

137
00:09:21,890 --> 00:09:22,750
Stop. Stop. Stop.

138
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:24,500
Put it back. Put it back.

139
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:25,650
How do you know all this?

140
00:09:25,770 --> 00:09:27,550
Didn't you tell me
to move into management?

141
00:09:27,550 --> 00:09:28,470
I studied it.

142
00:09:30,770 --> 00:09:31,410
Come on. Come on.

143
00:09:31,410 --> 00:09:32,240
Let's have a drink, man.

144
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:32,550
Sure.

145
00:09:32,550 --> 00:09:33,030
I'm telling you,

146
00:09:33,030 --> 00:09:35,270
you're young and promising.

147
00:09:35,270 --> 00:09:36,980
The future belongs to you young people.

148
00:09:36,980 --> 00:09:37,920
Come on, come on.

149
00:09:38,340 --> 00:09:39,010
All right, all right, all right.

150
00:09:39,010 --> 00:09:39,600
Mr. Liu,

151
00:09:39,650 --> 00:09:40,820
I enjoy drinking with you.

152
00:09:40,820 --> 00:09:41,750
Do you know that?

153
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:42,750
Bottoms up. Bottoms up! Bottoms up!

154
00:09:42,750 --> 00:09:43,570
I'm drinking it all.

155
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:44,630
Come on, come on.

156
00:09:44,630 --> 00:09:45,500
Let's not hang out with him any more.

157
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:46,130
Not any more.

158
00:09:46,130 --> 00:09:47,600
And what's with those...

159
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,320
those little glasses?

160
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:50,580
Let me take them off.

161
00:09:50,770 --> 00:09:51,270
Take them off.

162
00:09:51,270 --> 00:09:52,080
Let me try them on.

163
00:09:53,010 --> 00:09:53,670
Let me try them on.

164
00:09:53,670 --> 00:09:55,480
If you ever need anything, if you ever...

165
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,290
Don't hesitate to ask.

166
00:09:57,290 --> 00:09:58,370
Come on, come on.
Bottoms up.

167
00:09:58,370 --> 00:09:59,120
Bottoms up.

168
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:18,580
Look who's here!

169
00:10:26,530 --> 00:10:27,530
Mr. Liu, you're here.

170
00:10:27,530 --> 00:10:29,110
It's been a while since you've come by.

171
00:10:29,270 --> 00:10:30,850
Been busy lately?

172
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:32,240
Not too bad.

173
00:10:33,510 --> 00:10:34,670
I'm working the late shift tonight.

174
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:36,370
You go on home.

175
00:10:38,340 --> 00:10:40,220
Mr. Liu came to celebrate your birthday.

176
00:10:40,220 --> 00:10:40,750
Go on,

177
00:10:40,750 --> 00:10:41,650
I'll keep an eye on things here.

178
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:42,410
Thanks.

179
00:10:42,410 --> 00:10:43,150
No problem.

180
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:54,690
This is made of sugar.

181
00:10:56,650 --> 00:10:57,570
No way.

182
00:10:57,590 --> 00:10:59,520
That's what the cake seller told me.

183
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:04,240
It's sticky, isn't it?

184
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:18,100
Thank you.

185
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:19,790
You're welcome.

186
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:23,540
I have something else.

187
00:11:25,650 --> 00:11:26,580
Close your eyes.

188
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:33,730
Okay.

189
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:38,700
Do you like it?

190
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:44,810
This is for kids to wear.

191
00:11:45,010 --> 00:11:46,890
Who cares if it's for kids or adults?

192
00:11:47,550 --> 00:11:48,200
We'll wear it anyway.

193
00:11:48,650 --> 00:11:49,900
It's for good luck, right?

194
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:52,030
For safety and good fortune. Right?

195
00:11:52,770 --> 00:11:53,360
Here.

196
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:07,410
So beautiful.

197
00:12:07,790 --> 00:12:09,940
What a big piece of gold! Looks great.

198
00:12:22,940 --> 00:12:23,700
Honey,

199
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:27,290
happy birthday.

200
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:51,580
Look.

201
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:52,700
How about this?

202
00:12:57,480 --> 00:12:58,630
Just have a little cake

203
00:12:58,650 --> 00:12:59,360
to mark the occasion.

204
00:12:59,740 --> 00:13:01,130
Okay? Just to mark the occasion.

205
00:13:31,270 --> 00:13:31,820
How about this?

206
00:13:32,650 --> 00:13:34,570
I'll take you home first later,

207
00:13:35,650 --> 00:13:36,410
okay?

208
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:39,010
Take me home?

209
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,810
Aren't you coming home with me?

210
00:13:46,250 --> 00:13:48,500
I'll definitely
be home early tonight, okay?

211
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:54,070
Look, I just wanna earn more.

212
00:13:54,340 --> 00:13:55,390
By selling yourself?

213
00:13:55,390 --> 00:13:55,860
What?

214
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:57,080
By selling yourself?

215
00:14:01,710 --> 00:14:03,010
D-Don't be mad.

216
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:08,910
I won't go, okay?

217
00:14:24,410 --> 00:14:25,790
He said he's not going!

218
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:26,960
Stop calling him!

219
00:14:29,980 --> 00:14:33,870
[Literary Novel]

220
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:31,010
Look at him.

221
00:14:31,010 --> 00:14:32,690
Does he look like someone
who has a respectable job?

222
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:33,750
Exactly.

223
00:14:34,130 --> 00:14:35,100
If you ask me,

224
00:14:35,100 --> 00:14:36,840
the three of them
should just live together.

225
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:38,890
One's on days, one's on nights.

226
00:14:38,910 --> 00:14:40,380
The day and night shifts...

227
00:14:42,420 --> 00:14:43,300
Sorry.

228
00:15:19,650 --> 00:15:20,510
Come on, come on.

229
00:15:20,510 --> 00:15:21,510
Mr. Liu,

230
00:15:21,510 --> 00:15:22,550
let me raise a glass to you.

231
00:15:22,550 --> 00:15:24,120
I've heard you can really
hold your liquor.

232
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:25,370
Seeing is believing.

233
00:15:25,370 --> 00:15:26,000
Let me raise a glass to you.

234
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:30,700
Mr. Wang,

235
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:31,760
hear me out.

236
00:15:32,700 --> 00:15:33,790
You can train yourself
to hold your liquor,

237
00:15:34,510 --> 00:15:36,130
but business isn't won by drinking.

238
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:39,550
You're right, Mr. Liu.

239
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:42,150
Drinking is just to liven things up.

240
00:15:42,150 --> 00:15:43,510
What matters in business is sincerity.

241
00:15:43,510 --> 00:15:45,360
That's why I brought

242
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:46,960
my little hostess squad here today.

243
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:48,340
Ladies, raise a glass to Mr. Liu.

244
00:15:48,340 --> 00:15:49,320
Mr. Liu,

245
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,220
have a drink.

246
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:51,050
Have a drink, Mr. Liu.

247
00:15:51,050 --> 00:15:51,960
-Bottoms up.
-Mr. Liu.

248
00:15:52,150 --> 00:15:52,990
Cheers.

249
00:15:57,750 --> 00:15:58,370
Hey, come here.

250
00:15:58,580 --> 00:15:59,010
Me?

251
00:15:59,010 --> 00:15:59,670
Come here.

252
00:16:00,910 --> 00:16:02,080
Hey, girl.

253
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:03,630
Go, go, over there.

254
00:16:07,620 --> 00:16:08,460
What are you getting at?

255
00:16:12,650 --> 00:16:13,640
Man,

256
00:16:14,620 --> 00:16:16,550
our factory has all kinds of equipment,

257
00:16:16,970 --> 00:16:18,000
big and small,

258
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:20,460
and they all need your lubricants,

259
00:16:20,820 --> 00:16:21,710
right?

260
00:16:21,750 --> 00:16:22,980
You make quite a bit off us

261
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:24,580
over the course of a year, don't you?

262
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:27,790
What are you getting at?

263
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:28,720
Just say it.

264
00:16:29,630 --> 00:16:30,890
Our old machines don't need oil

265
00:16:30,890 --> 00:16:32,530
that's this high-quality, do they?

266
00:16:33,010 --> 00:16:35,370
You could lower the quality a little.

267
00:16:35,910 --> 00:16:37,260
I'm the one
in charge of purchasing, aren't I?

268
00:16:38,950 --> 00:16:40,550
Getting payments through the bank

269
00:16:40,750 --> 00:16:42,040
is a hassle.

270
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:44,640
Cash would be much more convenient.

271
00:16:47,980 --> 00:16:48,530
Look,

272
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:50,320
I brought it all with me.

273
00:16:51,530 --> 00:16:53,580
Is this all for us, or...

274
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:54,550
is there a cut for you, too?

275
00:16:55,790 --> 00:16:57,150
Come on.

276
00:16:57,150 --> 00:16:59,200
It's all yours.

277
00:16:59,630 --> 00:17:00,320
How could I trouble you

278
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:02,150
to transfer my share back to me,

279
00:17:02,150 --> 00:17:02,810
right?

280
00:17:03,630 --> 00:17:04,160
Mr. Wang,

281
00:17:04,510 --> 00:17:05,750
I've only ever heard

282
00:17:05,750 --> 00:17:07,400
of the supplier
giving the buyer a kickback.

283
00:17:07,420 --> 00:17:08,839
This is a first for me.

284
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:10,349
You went looking
for a piece of the pie yourself.

285
00:17:10,349 --> 00:17:11,960
You make your own money,
and eat your own food.

286
00:17:12,030 --> 00:17:12,910
You know what they say:

287
00:17:13,750 --> 00:17:16,400
"every man for himself," right?

288
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:18,510
If we settle in cash,

289
00:17:18,920 --> 00:17:20,440
you can pocket a little something

290
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:21,599
on the side too,

291
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:22,380
can't you?

292
00:17:23,270 --> 00:17:24,720
Ladies,

293
00:17:24,980 --> 00:17:25,640
come on.

294
00:17:25,940 --> 00:17:27,569
Get dancing, get singing!

295
00:17:27,569 --> 00:17:28,770
Let's all raise a glass to Mr. Liu.

296
00:17:28,770 --> 00:17:31,270
-Mr. Liu, may your business prosper!
-Mr. Liu.

297
00:17:31,270 --> 00:17:31,610
Come on.

298
00:17:32,050 --> 00:17:33,380
Let's liven things up a little.

299
00:17:33,380 --> 00:17:34,140
Cheers.

300
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:36,680
-Cheers!
-Mr. Liu, may your business prosper!

301
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:38,270
Have a drink, Mr. Liu.

302
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:48,090
Mr. Liu,

303
00:17:48,310 --> 00:17:49,420
we should get together more often.

304
00:17:49,830 --> 00:17:51,790
What do you think of my hostess team?

305
00:17:52,290 --> 00:17:52,700
Good.

306
00:17:52,700 --> 00:17:53,480
Not bad, right?

307
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:54,180
I won't walk you out.

308
00:17:54,180 --> 00:17:55,070
-Hey.
-Okay.

309
00:17:55,570 --> 00:17:56,440
We're good brothers

310
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:57,380
-for life.
-All right, all right, all right.

311
00:17:57,380 --> 00:17:58,750
Take care. Take care.

312
00:17:59,740 --> 00:18:00,460
Goodbye.

313
00:18:00,460 --> 00:18:02,030
Mr. Liu, Ms. Chen wants to see you.

314
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:06,250
We're brothers for life.

315
00:18:29,790 --> 00:18:30,770
Look at you.

316
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:33,030
You're even calling in hookers now.

317
00:18:35,140 --> 00:18:36,140
Keep this up,

318
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:37,270
and you won't even

319
00:18:37,270 --> 00:18:38,480
remember your own name.

320
00:18:38,770 --> 00:18:40,940
I was just helping you
maintain a client relationship.

321
00:18:41,310 --> 00:18:42,480
It's all just an act.

322
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:46,920
So should I thank you,

323
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:47,740
Mr. Liu?

324
00:18:50,380 --> 00:18:51,580
What about me?

325
00:18:53,460 --> 00:18:56,290
Were you just putting on an act
with your dying wife,

326
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:59,460
or with me?

327
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:22,070
When it comes to putting on an act,

328
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:24,520
who could possibly do it better than you?
